program	try_routing_clause_refusals.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	`try!` cannot take a routing clause — `try!` does not propagate the error, so there is no error channel to convert
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: `try!` cannot take a routing clause — `try!` does not propagate the error, so there is no error channel to convert"
log	"  --> examples/try_routing_clause_refusals.saw:63:5"
log	"     |"
log	" 63 |     try!(as LocalError.Alloc) grab(n)"
log	"     |     ^"
log	"   hint: drop the `(as LocalError.Alloc)`, or write a propagating `try` if the error should leave this function"
log	""
log	"error: `try?` cannot take a routing clause — `try?` does not propagate the error, so there is no error channel to convert"
log	"  --> examples/try_routing_clause_refusals.saw:67:5"
log	"     |"
log	" 67 |     try?(as LocalError.Alloc) grab(n)"
log	"     |     ^"
log	"   hint: drop the `(as LocalError.Alloc)`, or write a propagating `try` if the error should leave this function"
log	""
log	"error: a `try` with a routing clause cannot also carry a `catch` — route the error onward, or handle it here, not both"
log	"  --> examples/try_routing_clause_refusals.saw:71:13"
log	"     |"
log	" 71 |     let a = try(as LocalError.Alloc) grab(n) catch { 0 }"
log	"     |             ^"
log	"   hint: drop the `(as ...)` clause to handle the error in the `catch`, or drop the `catch` to route it to the caller"
log	""
log	"error: `try(as NotAnEnum.Alloc)`: `NotAnEnum` is not an enum in scope — a routing clause names an enum case"
log	"  --> examples/try_routing_clause_refusals.saw:76:12"
